  "val.explain": "The <b>Buffett Indicator</b> = total stock-market capitalization ÷ GDP × 100. It is a long-term equity-market <b>valuation context</b> measure — a big-picture gauge of how richly a whole market is valued relative to the size of its economy. It is slow-moving and is not a timing tool.",
